yaml/number
description: Number in one of six concretes
- >
  A number is a plain scalar in one of six concretes — decimal, hexadecimal, octal, binary,
  infinity, or not-a-number. See the subchapters below:
- !!<format: text/x-yaml> |
  a: 42
  b: 3.14e2
  c: 0x2A
  d: 0o52
  e: 0b101010
  f: .inf
  g: .nan
- *: 00-yaml_number_decimal
- *: 01-yaml_number_hexadecimal
- *: 02-yaml_number_octal
- *: 03-yaml_number_binary
- *: 04-yaml_number_infinity
- *: 05-yaml_number_nan
